<BaseLayout title="Active Directory and Identity Lab | Eric Bello" description="Windows Server and Active Directory home lab by Eric Bello.">
  <section class="project-hero shell narrow">
    <div class="project-meta"><span>Infrastructure and identity</span><span>Windows Server · AD DS · Networking</span></div>
    <h1>Active Directory and Identity Lab</h1>
    <p>A virtualized Windows Server environment built to practice the identity, access, networking, policy, and support tasks common to real IT environments.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="case-study shell narrow">
    <div class="case-section"><h2>Overview</h2><p>I configured Windows Server with Active Directory Domain Services and built out users, groups, organizational units, and Group Policy to model a small business environment.</p></div>
    <div class="case-section"><h2>Environment</h2><ul class="detail-list"><li>Windows Server and Active Directory Domain Services</li><li>DNS and DHCP services</li><li>Organizational units and security groups</li><li>Group Policy deployment and testing</li><li>Virtualized Windows clients through VMware Fusion</li></ul></div>
    <div class="case-section"><h2>What I practiced</h2><ul class="detail-list"><li>User and group administration</li><li>Password resets and account provisioning</li><li>Policy assignment and validation</li><li>Domain client configuration</li><li>Access and network troubleshooting workflows</li></ul></div>
    <div class="case-section emphasis"><h2>What this demonstrates</h2><p>Windows administration, identity management, DNS and DHCP fundamentals, Group Policy, access control, and the ability to work methodically through common infrastructure and support tasks.</p></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
